<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Švitrigaila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1370–1452</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Svidrigailo, Świdrygiełło</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Švitrigaila was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algirdas">Algirdas</a> and Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1430 to 1432. Supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Ruthenian nobles, he was overthrown by Sigismund Kęstutaitis and fought a civil war until his defeat at Wiłkomierz in 1435. He later ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a> as duke until his death in 1452, after which it was turned into a voivodeship of the Grand Duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/svitrigaila.jpg" alt="Švitrigaila" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alessandro Guagnini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Svitrigaila_(118503655).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
